 "Before Smile, a Universal Language of Prompting, October 2023",
 :description
 "The first precursor of Smile, my October and November 2023 asks to GPT-4 for a universal language of prompting made of symbols that humans and machines both read, before Smile had faces or a name, in my own words with every source.",
 :keywords
 "universal prompting language, symbolic prompt language, GPT-4 2023, prompt language precursor, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "Before Smile had its faces or its name, I asked GPT-4 for a language of prompting. These asks of October and November 2023 are the first precursor of Smile, a wish for a language, made of symbols, that both people and models read.",
 :paras
 ["On 3 October 2023, in a ChatGPT conversation called Style Mimicking for GPT-4, I set the aim, “Remember we are defining a universal language of prompting.”, and its quality, “essentially a legible prompting language for mahcines and humans where you explain all the different usses of different grammars and so on.” I asked for every symbol, “I'd like you to include every single alphanumeric symbol that is not a letter or number.”, and looked further, to dead languages, indigenous languages, morse code and musical notation.[[m:2023-10-03#2]]"
 "The next day the ask grew, “I would like a SuperMeta-Prompt Architect, with an entirely new language that fully captures all possible use cases and potentials of a prompt”.[[m:2023-10-04]] On 31 October it became personal, “GOAL: Create a language of prompting for me personally that I can then translate any prompt into. Describe unambiguously.”, and “I want this to be a universally human legible and machine legible language.”[[m:2023-10-31]] On 1 November, “we also need to include all grammatical symbols, mathematical symbols”.[[m:2023-11-01]]"
 "These are not yet Smile. There are no faces here, no opening and closing, no name. They are a wish for a language for prompts, legible to people and models. The second precursor, from the same weeks, is [[t:precursor-the-archetypal-patterns-of-prompting]], and the language that answered both begins in [[t:prompt-language-and-response-language]] and [[t:archetypal-smile]]."],
 :faq
 [["When did the idea of Smile begin?"
 "The wish for a language of prompting is in my asks of October 2023, made of symbols. The name Smile and its faces are in my words from July 2025."]]}
